// b4: a BMap from a Sorted batch in O(n), built bottom-up one level at a time. A level of r entries becomes nodes of
// 2 to 4 children: r = 1, 2, 3 give one B2, B3, B4; r >= 4 gives a B3, promotes the next key and goes on with r - 3 >= 1
// entries, so every leaf is at one depth. Each pass takes the first entry as its own argument (a group is never empty)
// and the passes alternate direction, so no level is reversed. The order of a level is in its type:
// BLvlA = the leftmost tree, then ascending BKT (a key and the tree right of it);
// BLvlD = descending BTK (a key and the tree left of it), then the rightmost tree.
enum Coll.BKT [V: Type]:
  case Coll.BKT(k: I64, v: V, t: Coll.BTree[V])

